1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,616
Official letters are hard to understand.

2
00:00:02,616 --> 00:00:06,016
And they are the last thing you should paste into a chatbot.

3
00:00:06,966 --> 00:00:11,424
Your name, your address, your tax number and your bank account, all on one page.

4
00:00:12,374 --> 00:00:17,825
Paperwork Decoder is for anyone facing a tax, bank or government letter they cannot follow.

5
00:00:17,825 --> 00:00:22,916
It hides who you are on your own device, then asks the cloud to explain what is left.

6
00:00:23,866 --> 00:00:30,302
It is built on Firebase AI Logic hybrid inference. Each feature chooses where it runs.

7
00:00:30,302 --> 00:00:36,290
Private steps run on the on-device model only. Reasoning runs in the cloud only.

8
00:00:36,290 --> 00:00:39,284
And quick help runs on the device first.

9
00:00:40,234 --> 00:00:43,597
Here is the app, with Gemini Nano ready inside Chrome.

10
00:00:43,597 --> 00:00:45,528
I will use a sample tax notice.

11
00:00:46,478 --> 00:00:54,010
Gemini Nano, running in the browser, finds the name, the address, the taxpayer number, the bank account and the phone.

12
00:00:54,010 --> 00:00:58,861
This is the exact text that will be sent. Nothing has left the computer yet.

13
00:00:58,861 --> 00:01:01,478
And I can hide or reveal anything myself.

14
00:01:02,428 --> 00:01:05,290
Now the cloud model gets the redacted letter.

15
00:01:05,290 --> 00:01:10,633
It says what this is, that it is urgent, the two things I can do, and the deadlines.

16
00:01:10,633 --> 00:01:17,057
My real bank reference is back in the answer. The cloud returned a label, and my device filled it in.

17
00:01:18,007 --> 00:01:26,955
Here is the receipt. About a thousand characters of redacted text went to the cloud, and ten personal details stayed on the device.

18
00:01:26,955 --> 00:01:30,301
Quick help uses the third mode, prefer on-device.

19
00:01:30,301 --> 00:01:35,561
This simpler explanation came from the local model, instantly and at no cost.

20
00:01:36,511 --> 00:01:37,762
It also drafts a reply.

21
00:01:37,762 --> 00:01:42,548
The cloud writes it with placeholders, and my reference numbers are added on the device.

22
00:01:43,498 --> 00:01:47,992
The same app runs natively on Android, with the same Firebase SDK.

23
00:01:47,992 --> 00:01:52,621
This emulator has no Gemini Nano, so it shows the designed fallback.

24
00:01:52,621 --> 00:01:58,545
Details are hidden by patterns, the app says so, and the cloud explanation still works.

25
00:01:59,495 --> 00:02:03,638
Paperwork Decoder. Two models, each doing the job it is suited to.

26
00:02:03,638 --> 00:02:06,275
Your letter explained, your identity kept.

